## Hunk 4 — show per-mint progress in the done-step UI (lines ~969–973)

```diff
 							{#if restoreStatus === 'running'}
 								<Body size="sm" color="secondary">{$_('recovery.restore.running')}</Body>
+								{#if restoreProgress}
+									<Body size="sm" color="secondary">{restoreProgress}</Body>
+								{/if}
 							{:else if restoreStatus === 'done'}
```

---

### Behavior change summary

- Before: `restoreFunds()` called `getActiveMintUrl()` once and restored only
  the single active mint.
- After: `restoreFunds()` calls `getAllMintConfigs()` and restores every
  configured mint (`restoreWallet()` per mint URL per active keyset), with an
  honest per-mint progress string (`{i}/{n}: {name|url}`) surfaced in the UI.
